From 6cb4d8908c35e1a23255b7b80fd3f8a247dad7cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:50:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Events: hidden booths, per-category free ordering, loyalty
 capture, paid beans
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Event stores are now QR-only and support a mixed free/paid menu:

- Hide event stores from the 'Choose your store' picker (default for the Event
  type; per-store toggle). They stay reachable by their ?loc= booth QR and
  resolve normally, but never appear as a choosable store.

- Per-event-store free categories: tick which categories are complimentary
  (coffee, tea). Those show NO price anywhere — menu tiles, item sheet, cart and
  checkout all read 'Complimentary' — and route to the kitchen for $0. Every
  other category (e.g. retail beans) stays a normal PAID item. Server classifies
  each line authoritatively from the Square catalog (never trusts the client),
  100%-discounting only the free lines; an all-free cart is a whole-order comp.

- First event order captures name + mobile, enrols the walk-up into Square
  loyalty, and the app remembers them on the device for one-tap reorders.

- Paid beans at an event: delivery address + a flat shipping fee (settings,
  default $10) added as a Square service charge, address on the kitchen ticket,
  charged through Square as normal.

- Every Event borrows a configurable default 'Visit us' store page (e.g. the
  Mitchell Roastery) so guests learn where to find the cafe afterwards.

New settings: eventDefaultStorePageLocId, eventShippingFee. Per-location:
freeCategories[], hidden. Admin Locations tab gains the controls for all of it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0187Jj4Q77V4UPawzEh9gsGr
